--- `concat` given one list written down joins its items, whatever the
--- two-piece concat joins: lists, text, tensors; a list of bytes held in
--- a variable too. Both modes print the same.
use math
log[concat[[[1, 2], [3], [4, 5]]]]
log[concat[['ab', 'cd', 'ef']]]
a = [1.0, 2.0]
b = [3.0]
log[concat[[a, b, [4.0]]]]
log[len[concat[[['x'], ['y', 'z']]]]]
log[concat[['only']]]
